I have a 166 Mhz DEC Multia with 64M ram in it. Originally I had
installed RH 4.2 on it, and it worked well until I stowed it away in the
closet. I recently decided to put it back in service, so I tried to
install (not upgrade to) RH 6.0 to bring it up to date. I encountered
some problems that I didn't see mentioned in the newsgroup archives on
Deja - hopefully someone can help me.

During the installation, the install process would hang for long periods
of time while installing packages. The stalls would sometimes be 10-12
hours long (in exhasperation, I left the machine sit). At first I
thought this was due to using the FTP install method, but the same thing
occured when installing from CD-ROM. I could switch VTs, but the switch
occured very slowly, and simple commands (eg. 'cat
/mnt/tmp/install.log') issued to the command line would take minutes to
hours to complete.

At long last, the install completed. When I restarted the machine, it
went into molasses mode when init started. Up until that point, the
kernel messages flew by as fast as 2.0.x ever did and no errors
appeared. I never did make it to a shell prompt.

Has anyone else experienced this? I've tried re-seating the memory and
ribbon cables. What else should I try?

