Runs Linux great, switch the console from AlphaBIOS to SRM, while powering
up hit F2, which will get you into setup. select  "cmos changes" then type
F6 "Advanced" selections, tab 3/4 the was down the screen and use the pull
down menu to select SRM Unix.     Then type F10 to save changes. finish up
by power cycling the system, it will restart with the SRM console enabled.
(To go back to AlphaBIOS, at the SRM prompt ">>>"  type:  set os_type nt
and power cycle,)

Then go to the Compaq web site

http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/linux/install_guide.html

And follow the directions for DS20,  (All SRM installs are the same)   The
main point to remember if using RH6, download the latest ramdisk image.
And use the generic kernel  from

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/

I have the best luck with generic-up-223.gz, After you complete the install
download the 2.2.11 sources from ftp.us.kernel.org and build your SMP
kernel.  I found the 2.2.11 to be very stable.

The only problem you may have is if your Graphics card is not supported,
Check the Compaq hhtp above, there's a list of hardware that was tested. A
halt during boot is the common symptom.

JJ






