I thought I'd post the solution to my problem, in case it can be of any
help to anyone.

My original post may not have been clear: Trying the SVGA server was a
desperation move.  In general, I had been attempting to use the TGA
server, which was included on the Alpha Debian distribution CDs.  The
problem was one of coming up with a modeline in XF86Config that would
support my card and monitor.  I found what I needed at
http://alphalinux.org - which is where I should have been looking in the
first place, but I was suffering from a mild attack of luseritis at the
time.

Alphalinux.org eventually linked me to
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/X11/XF86_TGA-3.1.2-README
which is a sample XF86Config file written by Jay Estabrook that works
with the ZLXp card. It only needed minor tweaking for the benefit of the
monitor.  One further change was needed before X would start: the mouse
device needed to be set to /dev/psaux.  I don't know if this is because
my mouse was otherwise misconfigured or if its a peculiarity of the AS
250.

Thank you to everyone who responded.

-- Chris Csernica



