On Wed, 18 Aug 1999, Ben Rusiecki wrote:

[SNIP]

>This time I just tried to boot off of the hard drive but it stopped soon
>after with a "aboot>" prompt waiting for me to type in some sort of boot
>parameters.

It means all is well, aboot (for booting from the SRM console) is
installed correctly. It displays the interactive boot prompt because the
boot_osflags nvram parameter contains the letter i(nteractive). If you'd
set them to something like "root=/dev/sda2 ro" or whatever you'd like
for a kernel command like, it should boot straight away. Alternatively,
you could enter your kernel command line here at the aboot prompt.

Hope this helps, and otherwise, there's also an excellent SRM firmware
HOWTO which also covers aboot at http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/srm.html.


