X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V4.72.3110.3
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha
X-Complaints-To: newsabuse@supernews.com

use a 2.2.* (11) kernel compiled with serial console support.  Follow the
instructions in the usr/src/linux/Documentation  directory, to recreate
/dev/console  with major minor device codes of 5, 1 and /dev/tty0 as 4, 0..

5,1 is the default console port. Installs just create a link from console to
tty0 or create console with tty0 device codes. tty0 is the first virtual
console (graphics).    When this is all done, If a graphics card is present,
Linux will use it as a default console.   If a Graphic card is not detected,
console will redirect automatically to ttyS0.

I use this feature all the time with the 2.2.3 and 2.2.11 kernels..

JJ

