Generic-smp-223.img does not support Redhat 6 's ramdisk format, which is romfs.

If you have RH6 CD, you can try specify CD-ROM as root, i.e.
P00>>> boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 load_ramdisk=1"

 Also you can try the generic.img from Redhat6, or an unofficial image at my
site.
ftp://mars.iol.unh.edu/pub/linux/images/2.2.10.img

Regards

