The steps are as the following:
 cd /usr/src
 rm linux
 tar xzvf /tmp/linux-2.2.11.tar.gz
 mv linux linux-2.2.11
 ln -s linux-2.2.11 linux
 cd /usr/src/linux
 make config           or   make   oldconfig
 make dep
 make clean            ( not necessary)
 make boot
 make modules
 make  modules_ install
cp /usr/src/linux-2.2.11/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz     /vmlinux.gz ( This
step copy the kernel image to the /vmlinux.gz. You should   change the kernel
path in the milo)
 cp /usr/src/linux-2.2.11/System.map   /boot/System.map-2.2.11
  cd /boot
  rm System.map
  ln -s System.map-2.2.11 System.map

Boot image is a compressed kernel.  After you follow the steps and change the
milo path, everything
will be OK. When you login, it will show the correct version. Or you can "do
cat   /proc/version "  It will show current versions of kernel and gcc.


Take care.


--
Xiaozhou Qiu

Linux Consorsium
Interoperability Lab
University of New Hampshire



