On Wed, 11 Aug 1999 09:36:58 -0400, Rick Brice wrote:
> IBM has removed or moved a lot of data....
> this is not the right size SIMM,
> but the theory is the same.
> The point you are missing is that the extra eight bits are fully mapped.
> 
> http://www.chips.ibm.com/products/memory/26H2528/

These are EOS SIMMs, not ECC SIMMs.
EOS SIMMs are SIMMs which perform internal error correction, but otherwise
behave like true parity SIMMs (x36) to the host system.
ECC SIMMs are SIMMs which perform internal error correction and behave like...
well..., ECC SIMMs (x40) to the host system.
These are not the same.

Greetings,

Ton.
