This question is *way* off topic for this group, but here's my feeling
on it:  unless you actually paid about $90 for Windows 98, the
technicial illegally installed a licensed program on your system and
you should take it back to the shop and demand that they remove it.
Take along your Win95 disc so they can fix the broken files.

As far as I know, you can't share Win95 and 98 on a system.  I'm not
sure why you'd want to since they are essentially the same operating
system.  I believe that if you upgrade a 95 system to 98, then 98
installs itself over the 95 installation.

Now, if the question were on topic, I'd note that if you were using
Linux this wouldn't be an issue because Linux isn't bound by silly
license agreements that nobody reads but which are intended to make
you pay $90 for essentially nothing (the upgrade from Win95 -> Win98).




