Malice is not relevant.

The author demonstrated remarkable ignorance.

SCSI is SCSI if you know what it is, you should know it supports
multiple devices.! Period!
If the UDB had no external SCSI port, it is a piece of cake to add the
port.
Any decent external SCSI box has two ports on it.
What did the author think the extra port was for?

If the author had read even a small part of the web based material that
is available about
the multia, he would know that IDE drives and IDE boot ARE supported.

ALSO, the multia does not use True Parity SIMMS!
The multia uses ECC SIMMS. 
It is PC Clone Ignorance that confuses the type of SIMM.
There is a wealth of information on the web about SIMMS,
many confuse Logical Parity with True Parity and often ECC SIMMS are
mistakenly call True Parity.
If you blindly order True Parity you may get either.
If it is too cheap, you most certainly will get the wrong memory.
The cheapest I've heard rumored for ECC is $96 for 64Mb.

I used the linux instructions and RAWRITE to create my MILO, and
failsafe loader
and had no problems.

My biggest gripe - I wish the TVGA was fully supported.

Regards,
Rick

