>> > 2) What are the little silver IC's that have a speed rating on them (25 ~
>> > 50Mhz) that came with the motherbaord?  And when should I use different
>> > speeds?
>> 
>> Eh?

>Yeah, still nothing on this one yet..

Are they by any chance square and have only 4 "pins", one in each corner?
If so, they are likely to be crystals rather than ICs. There should be
one of them in position U34, right next to the CPU (behind it and to the 
left when viewing from the direction of the power connector).

According to my manual, the default crystal is 36.666MHz. However, my 
board actually has a 43.333MHz in that position, and it runs at 433MHz.
So I suspect you'd want the 50MHz one for your 500MHz processor.

