> it picks
> up time rapidly.  The hardware clock is also bizarre.  It shows a date
> (via
> /sbin/clock) in 2019.

I assume it is a DPW 500a (500au's are DUNIX)
I have no idea how to slow the clock... Check that the clock setting in
the BIOS is correct and set ARC=true in /etc/sysconfig/clock
always use clock with the -A flag
Alternatively, upgrade to the new version of clock (clock-1.1-6) which
seems to detect the correct year offset.

- Alex



