> VX40's right?   I've seen some notes regarding UDB/Multia features
> and jumpers....
> 
> Can these VX40's be upgraded to 233 MHz by swapping for a faster
> Alpha 21066 (from starship, i assume) and changing jumpers...and
> perhaps improving the cooling situation by installing a more powerful
> fan (as the NetBSD pages suggest)  ??
> 
No.  The VX40 series has a fixed 256K cache and fixed 166MHz CPU.
If you are daring, you could jumper it faster - but I wouldn't
recommend it.

> Are the VX42 multia's the same motherboard as VX40's w/ just a faster
> processor?
> 
Basically. The VX40 is as described above, while the VX42 has a 512K
upgradeable cache and 233MHz ZIF socket CPU.

Depending on the rest of the product code, these boxes may or may not
come with HD, floppy, or PCI option card. Check the descriptions
carefully before you buy.

