Here's some instructions from the web.....
http://www.multimania.com/multia/miniide.html
This info is a bit dated....
As many old, junk, scrap, computer salvage, laptops as there are out
there,
you should be able to find a 44-pin laptop IDE cable for your 2.5"
drive.
Makes things a lot simpler.
IF not, you can buy one. (GASP!<G>)

If your UDB comes with a metal blank in the vacant floppy position,
a little cutting and drilling and you've got youself a mounting tray for
your IDE drive.
If not, it ain't rocket science to bend and make a little bracket.

I have another theory I haven't tested yet, but if I'm right some of you
are going to kick yourself and some are gonna be happy.
Here it is...
That SCSI controller without the PCI riser looks to me like it is
exactly the same as the one with the PCI riser.
Install the PCI riser connector and the mini-SCSI header and I'll bet
dollars to Dunkin' Donuts that they both work!
You can probably buy the headers from Tech America, etc.

Also remember, the UDB won't boot with a dead battery!
Batteries Plus and Radio Shack have replacements.
I bought a bigger one from Batteries Plus!
The correct voltage is all that matters.

Regards,
Rick



