Hm, I did follow the thread, and for all I recall, the effect was that
running fortran stuff on Alpha + Linux  was slower than Alpha + Tru64
Unix. This was stated (and accepted throughout the thread) as a fact,
and that something may change in the future doesn't mean too much for
someone who needs all the power right now.

I also read that that was attributed to the missing page coloring and
differences in the linker, and that DECompaq ponder doing something
about it. Nevertheless, the performance of Alpha + Linux was still
better than anything else out there (SPECfp in the 40s, compared to 58
or so for Alpha + Tru64), and, of course, I have no idea how that
translates to real-world performance for the given codes. Only
benchmarks with these codes can tell.

BTW, I find Linus thoughts quite interesting and would love to see what
the certainly equally competent folks from DECompaq think about all
that.

