There are (at least) three items on Tru64 UNIX not (yet) available on 
Linux that go into the SPEC results differences between Linux and Tru64;
not just page coloring. 

These are:
	Profiling/feedback from previous runs
	The KAP preprocessor from Kuch and Associates.
	Page coloring
See:
http://www.spec.org/osg/cpu95/flags/CompaqTru64_UNIX_990201.txt
for details of the switches do, and the SPEC results themselves
for the switches used for each test.

The compilers and the math library were just the first steps.  How much 
each of the items above contribute to the differences remain to be seen, 
though we may be able to get some data.  We did the low hanging fruit
here first, those that will benefit the most people the most quickly
by doing the compilers and math library.

Phil Ezolt may have some information along these lines.

So let's not jump to conclusions here: lets get data and see what
the effects of each really are....  But feel free to make Linus eat his
words; at least he doesn't write a column to eat the way Metcalfe did
around the Internet (and I'd like to persuade him to do likewise about
Linux) :-).
